  "id": "DrugBank_DB00175 - MONDO_2679",
  "verbalization": "Pravastatin is implicated in the pathogenesis of cerebral infarction through a series of interconnected pathways. The evidence suggests that Pravastatin may contribute to the risk of cerebral infarction via its role in hyperlipidemia, which is associated with atherosclerosis and vascular dysfunction. This is supported by the indication of Pravastatin with Hyperlipidemia, Familial Combined, Lpl Related, which in turn is linked to Rosuvastatin and Atorvastatin, both of which are known to increase low-density lipoprotein (LDL) cholesterol and promote atherosclerosis. The indirect pathway through Vorapaxar, which is indicated with Stroke Disorder and linked to cerebral infarction, adds another layer of complexity, suggesting that Pravastatin may influence vascular health through multiple mechanisms. The cumulative evidence highlights a potential role of Pravastatin in the development of cerebral infarction via lipid-related pathways, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated.",
